From: bentoo <noreply@obentoo.org>
Subject: [PATCH] sched/fair: BORE: cover update_protect_slice() on 7.3.1

Linux 7.3.1 backported a fair.c change that makes update_protect_slice()
read normalized_sysctl_sched_base_slice. The BORE patch for 7.3 (CachyOS
kernel-patches 68476639) only declares that variable without
CONFIG_SCHED_BORE, and already gives set_protect_slice() the BORE base
slice instead. Do the same here, so a BORE build compiles again.

Drop once CachyOS's 7.3 BORE patch handles this function.
---
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -1172,7 +1172,11 @@
 static inline void update_protect_slice(struct cfs_rq *cfs_rq, struct sched_entity *se)
 {
 	u64 vruntime = min_vruntime(se->vruntime, avg_vruntime(cfs_rq));
+#ifdef CONFIG_SCHED_BORE
+	u64 slice = sysctl_sched_base_slice;
+#else /* CONFIG_SCHED_BORE */
 	u64 slice = normalized_sysctl_sched_base_slice;
+#endif /* CONFIG_SCHED_BORE */
 	u64 vprot;
 
 	if (sched_feat(RUN_TO_PARITY))
